---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import ContactFooter from '../components/ContactFooter.astro';
import '@fontsource/bebas-neue/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/caveat/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/poppins/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/poppins/latin-500.css';
import '@fontsource/poppins/latin-600.css';
const steps = [['Issue','Jira / Azure'],['Design','AI + human review'],['Automate','Playwright / PyTest'],['Execute','CI pipeline'],['Evidence','Reports + logs'],['Sync','Xray / Test Plans']];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="Selected quality engineering case studies by Yash Chavda."/><meta name="theme-color" content="#f8f0e2"/><title>Selected Work — Yash Chavda</title></head><body class="work-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><Header current="projects" /><main id="main"><section class="work-section" id="work"><div class="wrap work-intro"><div class="section-top"><span class="section-label">01 / SELECTED WORK</span><span class="section-label">FOUR CASE STUDIES</span></div><p class="script">the proof</p><h1>WORK THAT<br/>WORKS<span class="red">.</span></h1><a class="section-next" href="#case-01" aria-label="Continue to the first case study"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><div class="case-grid">
<article class="case" id="case-01"><div class="case-content"><span class="case-index">CASE STUDY / 01</span><h3>AUTOMATION<br/>AT SCALE<span class="red">.</span></h3><p>Led test architecture and delivery on a large enterprise programme using Selenium C#, xUnit/BDD and Jenkins.</p><ul><li>Reusable framework and execution design</li><li>Flakiness triage, reviews and team coaching</li><li>On-site client enablement and handover</li></ul></div><div class="case-visual yellow"><span class="giant">4,000+</span><strong>AUTOMATED TESTS</strong><div class="visual-rule"></div><small>ENTERPRISE DELIVERY</small><b>FRAMEWORK + PIPELINE + PEOPLE</b></div><a class="section-next" href="#case-02" aria-label="Continue to case study 2"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></article>
<article class="case" id="case-02"><div class="case-content"><span class="case-index">CASE STUDY / 02</span><h3>PERFORMANCE<br/>IS A FEATURE<span class="red">.</span></h3><p>Built a K6 performance-testing framework and wired it into Azure DevOps with Grafana observability.</p><ul><li>Repeatable load scenarios</li><li>Pipeline execution and result reporting</li><li>Azure resource metrics alongside test results</li></ul></div><div class="case-visual teal"><small>LOAD LAB / PERFORMANCE</small><svg viewBox="0 0 300 120" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a rising performance load graph"><path d="M0 100H300 M0 60H300 M0 20H300" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".25"/><path d="M0 105 L35 98 L62 102 L88 75 L112 82 L145 49 L170 58 L201 30 L230 40 L260 12 L300 20" fill="none" stroke="#ffc64b" stroke-width="4"/></svg><strong>VIRTUAL USER LOAD</strong><b>k6 → AZURE → GRAFANA</b></div><a class="section-next" href="#case-03" aria-label="Continue to case study 3"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></article>
<article class="case" id="case-03"><div class="case-content"><span class="case-index">CASE STUDY / 03</span><h3>TESTING AI<br/>RESPONSIBLY<span class="red">.</span></h3><p>As the QA owner for a RAG-driven application, I tested more than API responses: retrieval relevance, grounding, context and answer quality.</p><div class="tags"><span>PYTEST</span><span>RAG</span><span>S3 / AZURE AI SEARCH</span></div></div><div class="case-visual chain"><small>THE EVALUATION CHAIN</small><div>01 &nbsp; DOCUMENT / CHUNKS</div><div>02 &nbsp; RETRIEVAL / CONTEXT</div><div>03 &nbsp; GROUNDED RESPONSE</div><b>ACCURACY · RELEVANCE · HALLUCINATION RISK</b></div><a class="section-next" href="#case-04" aria-label="Continue to case study 4"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></article>
<article class="case" id="case-04"><div class="case-content"><span class="case-index">CASE STUDY / 04</span><h3>A BETTER<br/>FRAMEWORK<span class="red">.</span></h3><p>Migrating from Cypress to Playwright was about maintainability, traceability and developer trust — not just a new API.</p></div><div class="case-visual transition"><div><small>BEFORE</small><strong>CYPRESS</strong><p>Existing suite / growing maintenance needs / reporting gaps</p></div><span class="transition-arrow">→</span><div><small>AFTER</small><strong>PLAYWRIGHT</strong><p>Page objects / CI pipelines / reliable reports / test case mapping</p></div></div><a class="section-next" href="#quality-loop" aria-label="Continue to the quality workflow"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></article></div></section>
<section class="section wrap system" id="quality-loop"><div class="section-top"><span class="section-label">02 / SYSTEMS I BUILD</span><span class="section-label">THE QUALITY LOOP</span></div><p class="script">from ticket</p><h2>TO TRUSTWORTHY<br/>SIGNAL<span class="red">.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">An AI-assisted QA loop: turn requirements into tests, execute in CI, and connect evidence back to the work.</p><div class="flow">{steps.map((step,i)=><div class="flow-step"><span>0{i+1}</span><h3>{step[0]}</h3><p>{step[1]}</p></div>)}</div><p class="principle"><strong>THE PRINCIPLE</strong> Automation should improve traceability and decisions — not simply produce more green checkmarks.</p><a class="section-next" href="/experiments/" aria-label="Continue to experiments"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></section>
<ContactFooter backHref="#main" /></main></body></html>